  "observations": [
    "All three original resize runs retain the stage43 failure, and all four host API calls occurred; coalescing alone cannot explain these samples.",
    "Replaying exactly the observed UI parser resizes and feed partitions reproduces the full live failed screen, not only the failing marker.",
    "The candidate grows the visible buffer by pulling history into it. In these samples the later host stream does not repaint the whole resized buffer, and its cursor-addressed echo and size output overwrite different existing rows.",
    "The native size helper output contains the independent TF_SIZE_100x28 result; no CHAR_INFO snapshot at this failure boundary was captured.",
    "Pinned host source already documents divergent host/terminal reflow and lazy DSR CPR synchronization at console-info queries. This is relevant source evidence, not proof of an exhaustive root cause or a completed fix."
  ],
